parameters.text:
=You are a meticulous travel operations quality analyst reviewing ground-supplier incident reports for a DMC reliability program.

Supplier: {{ $json.supplierName }} ({{ $json.supplierType }}) operating in {{ $json.destination }}
Reported Incident Type: {{ $json.incidentType }}
Reported By: {{ $json.reportedBy }}
Affected Passengers: {{ $json.affectedPax }}
Reported Delay (minutes): {{ $json.delayMinutesReported }}

Contractual SLA Terms:
{{ $json.slaTerms }}

Incident Description (raw, from tour operator / traveler):
{{ $json.incidentDescription }}

Additional Tour Operator Notes:
{{ $json.tourOperatorNotes }}

Your task:
1. Determine the true incident type and severity based on the actual description, not just the reported label.
2. Decide whether the SLA terms above were actually breached.
3. Identify the most likely root cause category.
4. Extract confirmed delay minutes and passengers affected if stated or implied in the description.
5. Note if the report is vague, contradictory, or lacks enough detail to score confidently.

Return a JSON object with EXACTLY these fields:
{
  "confirmedIncidentType": "Delay|Complaint|SLA Breach|No-Show|Quality Issue|Other",
  "severity": "Minor|Moderate|Severe|Critical",
  "slaBreached": true or false,
  "rootCauseCategory": "Supplier Fault|Force Majeure|Communication Failure|Traveler Error|Unclear",
  "delayMinutesConfirmed": <number>,
  "paxAffectedConfirmed": <number>,
  "incidentSummary": "Two to three sentence neutral summary of what happened",
  "extractionConfidence": <number 1-10, 10 = fully clear and verifiable report>
}

Return ONLY the JSON. No markdown, no explanation.

parameters.jsCode:
const item = $input.item.json;
let parsed = {};
try {
  const rawText = item.output || item.text || item.response || '{}';
  const clean = rawText.replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();
  parsed = JSON.parse(clean);
} catch(e) {
  parsed = {
    confirmedIncidentType: item.incidentType,
    severity: 'Moderate',
    slaBreached: /sla/i.test(item.incidentType || ''),
    rootCauseCategory: 'Unclear',
    delayMinutesConfirmed: item.delayMinutesReported,
    paxAffectedConfirmed: item.affectedPax,
    incidentSummary: 'Auto-passed: could not parse AI classification output, trusting self-reported incident details.',
    extractionConfidence: 5
  };
}
return { json: { ...item, ...parsed } };

const item = $input.item.json;
const priorScore = (typeof item.priorReliabilityScore === 'number') ? item.priorReliabilityScore : 85;

// Base penalty by confirmed severity
const severityPenaltyMap = { Minor: 3, Moderate: 8, Severe: 16, Critical: 28 };
let penalty = severityPenaltyMap[item.severity] || 8;

// Additional penalty for a confirmed SLA breach
if (item.slaBreached === true || item.slaBreached === 'true') {
  penalty += 10;
}

// Root cause adjustment - supplier fault weighted fully, force majeure / traveler error reduce the penalty
const rootCause = item.rootCauseCategory || 'Unclear';
let rootCauseMultiplier = 0.9; // Unclear: slight benefit of the doubt
if (rootCause === 'Supplier Fault') rootCauseMultiplier = 1;
else if (rootCause === 'Communication Failure') rootCauseMultiplier = 0.8;
else if (rootCause === 'Force Majeure') rootCauseMultiplier = 0.3;
else if (rootCause === 'Traveler Error') rootCauseMultiplier = 0;

penalty = penalty * rootCauseMultiplier;

// Frequency penalty based on trailing 90-day incident rate
const totalIncidents = item.totalIncidentsLast90Days || 0;
const totalBookings = (item.totalBookingsLast90Days && item.totalBookingsLast90Days > 0) ? item.totalBookingsLast90Days : 1;
const incidentRatePercent = Math.round((totalIncidents / totalBookings) * 1000) / 10;
let frequencyPenalty = 0;
if (incidentRatePercent > 20) frequencyPenalty = 12;
else if (incidentRatePercent > 10) frequencyPenalty = 7;
else if (incidentRatePercent > 5) frequencyPenalty = 3;

// Small mean-reversion recovery pull toward 100, so suppliers already low aren't permanently locked out of recovering
const recoveryPull = priorScore < 100 ? Math.round((100 - priorScore) * 0.02) : 0;

const rawScore = priorScore - penalty - frequencyPenalty + recoveryPull;
const newReliabilityScore = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Math.round(rawScore)));
const scoreChange = Math.round((newReliabilityScore - priorScore) * 10) / 10;

let reliabilityTier = 'Excellent';
if (newReliabilityScore < 35) reliabilityTier = 'Critical / Non-Compliant';
else if (newReliabilityScore < 55) reliabilityTier = 'At Risk';
else if (newReliabilityScore < 75) reliabilityTier = 'Watch List';
else if (newReliabilityScore < 90) reliabilityTier = 'Reliable';

return {
  json: {
    ...item,
    incidentRatePercent,
    penaltyApplied: Math.round(penalty * 10) / 10,
    frequencyPenaltyApplied: frequencyPenalty,
    recoveryPullApplied: recoveryPull,
    newReliabilityScore,
    scoreChange,
    reliabilityTier
  }
};

parameters.text:
=You are a DMC / ground-supplier performance manager producing a recommendation for a human procurement or operations lead, not an automated termination decision.

Supplier: {{ $json.supplierName }} ({{ $json.supplierType }}) - {{ $json.destination }}
Incident Type: {{ $json.confirmedIncidentType }} | Severity: {{ $json.severity }} | SLA Breached: {{ $json.slaBreached }}
Root Cause: {{ $json.rootCauseCategory }}
Incident Summary: {{ $json.incidentSummary }}

Prior Reliability Score: {{ $json.priorReliabilityScore }}/100
New Reliability Score: {{ $json.newReliabilityScore }}/100 ({{ $json.reliabilityTier }})
Score Change This Incident: {{ $json.scoreChange }}
Trailing 90-Day Incident Rate: {{ $json.incidentRatePercent }}% ({{ $json.totalIncidentsLast90Days }} incidents / {{ $json.totalBookingsLast90Days }} bookings)

Guidance: Critical/Non-Compliant or At Risk tiers combined with a Supplier Fault root cause should generally lean toward Probation or Terminate/Replace. Watch List tier or a Communication Failure root cause can lean toward Formal Warning with specific corrective actions. Reliable or Excellent tiers with an isolated, low-severity incident can lean toward Monitor or Retain. Always ground your reasoning in the actual numbers above.

Return a JSON object with EXACTLY these fields:
{
  "recommendation": "Retain|Monitor|Formal Warning|Probation|Terminate/Replace",
  "reasoning": "Two to four sentences referencing the specific numbers above",
  "correctiveActions": ["action1", "action2"],
  "requiresContractReview": true or false,
  "recommendationConfidence": <number 0-100>
}

If no corrective actions apply, return an empty array. Return ONLY the JSON. No markdown, no explanation.

parameters.jsCode:
const item = $input.item.json;
let parsed = {};
try {
  const rawText = item.output || item.text || item.response || '{}';
  const clean = rawText.replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();
  parsed = JSON.parse(clean);
} catch(e) {
  parsed = {
    recommendation: 'Monitor',
    reasoning: 'Auto-flagged: could not parse AI recommendation output, routing to Monitor with a contract review as a precaution.',
    correctiveActions: [],
    requiresContractReview: true,
    recommendationConfidence: 50
  };
}
return { json: { ...item, ...parsed } };

const item = $input.item.json;
const recordedAt = new Date().toISOString();

return {
  json: {
    ...item,
    recordedAt,
    scorecardSummaryRow: [
      item.incidentId || 'N/A',
      item.supplierId || '',
      item.supplierName || '',
      item.supplierType || '',
      item.destination || '',
      item.confirmedIncidentType || '',
      item.severity || '',
      item.slaBreached ? 'Yes' : 'No',
      item.rootCauseCategory || '',
      item.priorReliabilityScore || 0,
      item.newReliabilityScore || 0,
      item.scoreChange || 0,
      item.reliabilityTier || '',
      item.recommendation || '',
      JSON.stringify(item.correctiveActions || []),
      recordedAt
    ]
  }
};

